Place your SSL/TLS certificates here.

EMQX does not ship certificate files.  On first start, EMQX generates a
unique self-signed certificate (managed-certs bundle named `localhost`,
stored under `data/certs2/global/localhost/`) which the default `ssl`
and `wss` listeners use.  When a node joins a cluster, it inherits the
cluster's bundle instead.

The generated certificate identity is:

- Server certificate: `CN=localhost, O=EMQX`, with SAN entries for
  `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, and `::1`.
- It is signed by a one-off `CN=EMQX Self-Signed CA` whose key is
  discarded after signing.

Self-signed certificates are only suitable for testing and local
deployments.  For production, place certificates issued for your own
environment in this directory (or anywhere readable by EMQX) and point
the listener configuration at them, for example:

  listeners.ssl.default {
    ssl_options {
      certfile = "etc/certs/cert.pem"
      keyfile = "etc/certs/key.pem"
      cacertfile = "etc/certs/cacert.pem"
    }
  }

Alternatively, upload certificates via the Dashboard or the `/certs`
HTTP API to have them replicated across the cluster as managed-certs
bundles.
